# GitHub Linguist fallback highlighting until native VibeLang support lands.
*.yb linguist-language=Rust
*.vibe linguist-language=Rust

# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows checkouts.
#
# Without this, a Windows runner with core.autocrlf=true checks source out with
# CRLF, and every raw string literal that spans lines then contains a bare CR.
# Rust rejects that outright: `error: bare CR not allowed in string, use \r
# instead`. That is what broke package-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc, and because the
# packaging job failed, the signing, SBOM, reproducibility and install-smoke
# jobs downstream of it were skipped -- which is why no release since v1.0.0
# carries a single attached asset. 39 .rs files in this repo contain `r#"`
# literals, so the exposure is broad rather than incidental.
#
# Every file is already stored with LF, so this pins existing behaviour on the
# platforms that were fine and repairs the one that was not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.tar binary
*.wasm binary
*.o binary
*.a binary
*.dylib binary
*.so binary
*.exe binary
